  <p class="note">Read from plan.json: 52 open groups, 45 merge batches, closure 2026-10-30T08:03:00Z. A wave is the set of groups dispatched at one instant; the next opens as soon as one of the six pull-request slots frees, so waves overlap and the cap is never exceeded. At most two PLANNED groups in flight touch coordinator.py; the 3 inherited in-progress coordinator groups are recorded in plan.json (cap 2, no coordinator pull request measured open). The line above the lanes is how many groups are in flight at each hour, riding the cap. Stamps: one patch per five production groups, the minor at closure; no stamp blocks a dispatch. Hover any bar, however narrow, for its name, state, start, ETA and wave. 6 of 11 critical-path links are drawn; the ◆ and the caption carry the rest.</p>
