    <tbody id="rows"><tr class="done" data-st="done"><td class="g">ARCHSCORE-COVERAGE<div class="lanec">Instruments</div></td><td class="d">Fold the arch seats&#x27; leads into the archscore, one group on tools/audit/archscore/.</td><td><span class="pill done">merged at acfeaf8b</span></td><td class="mono">merged</td><td><span class="chip" title="[R10-N-name-sort] An entity family&#x27;s display names do not lead with a shared token, so the name sort Home Assistant and the card use splits the family, per language">#2228</span><span class="chip" title="[R10-N-structure-blind] A structural ratchet or dead-code metric measures a name or regex proxy instead of the property it gates, so dead production members or cross-seam coupling pass it unmeasured">#2235</span><span class="chip closer" title="[R10-ARCHSCORE-COVERAGE] archscore coverage: layering, card script, dict-literal clones, hub aliases, ARCH-s3 holes, shape census, event-callback writes">#2259</span></td><td class="blk">—</td><td class="mono">—</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr class="done" data-st="done"><td class="g">D15-GRADER<div class="lanec">Instruments</div></td><td class="d">(a) Re-key the three bundle pins in tools/policy/check-wave-script.mjs on D15&#x27;s brief existing, not on the bundle-dimensions declaration in the find workflow: today an em…</td><td><span class="pill done">merged at 63d8154c</span></td><td class="mono">merged</td><td><span class="chip" title="[R10-D15-GRADER] D15 graders: key the bundle pins on the brief existing; give M1 a restart-gap threshold">#2268</span></td><td class="blk">—</td><td class="mono">—</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr class="done" data-st="done"><td class="g">DEAD-RATE-LIMIT<div class="lanec">Core model</div></td><td class="d">Found by the R10-TRUST-RELATIVE seat (no defer): after that group&#x27;s relative trust region, the rate limit `HOUSE_LOSS_MAX_STEP` (the `max_step_fraction=HOUSE_LOSS_MAX_STE…</td><td><span class="pill done">merged at d4fb5351</span></td><td class="mono">merged</td><td>—</td><td class="blk">—</td><td class="mono">—</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr class="done" data-st="done"><td class="g">DEEPLINK<div class="lanec">Product UX</div></td><td class="d">The deep-link class (owner, 2026-10-14): one mechanism is broken in three places, Advisor &quot;Open settings&quot;, Setup &quot;Configure&quot; and Health &quot;Show&quot;.</td><td><span class="pill done">merged at 07c5c7c3</span></td><td class="mono">merged</td><td><span class="chip" title="[R10-P2] One fact decided twice by divergent predicates: a guard at one seam, missing at its sibling">#2238</span><span class="chip" title="[R10-DEEPLINK] Card deep links: one shared helper for options-flow step, filtered entity table and single entity">#2253</span></td><td class="blk">—</td><td class="mono">—</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr class="done" data-st="done"><td class="g">DEEPLINK-CENSUS<div class="lanec">Product UX</div></td><td class="d">Split from the R10-DEEPLINK pull request (#2283) after its round-4 review (verdict on head 1826c67c3), as issue #2317: the deep-link builder and its own checks are sound,…</td><td><span class="pill done">merged at f4955e15</span></td><td class="mono">merged</td><td><span class="chip" title="[R10-DEEPLINK] navigation census misses bare open(), Navigation API, form action and Event-built more-info">#2317</span></td><td class="blk">—</td><td class="mono">—</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr class="done" data-st="done"><td class="g">DIAG-REPLAY<div class="lanec">Replay</div></td><td class="d">Owner (tvofi, 2026-10-14): wire the export into Download diagnostics.</td><td><span class="pill done">merged at 0dac0bf8</span></td><td class="mono">merged</td><td><span class="chip" title="[R10-DIAG-REPLAY] Download diagnostics: fill the bundle&#x27;s replay half through the export&#x27;s allowlist and sanitiser">#2271</span></td><td class="blk">—</td><td class="mono">—</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr class="done" dat