<section>
  <h2>How the ETAs are computed</h2>
  <p class="note">Every figure on this page is <code>plan.json</code>'s, written by <code>tools/plan/replan.py</code>; this renderer draws it and computes no schedule of its own. A wave is the set of groups dispatched at one moment, and the next opens as soon as one of six pull-request slots frees, so a wave never waits for the previous one to drain; the cap limits concurrency, not the wave boundary. Duration is dispatch to merge by roster size, from <code>tools/plan/durations.json</code>: S 13.1 h, M 11.4 h, L 20.1 h, XL 30.2 h, the median lead time of done round-10 groups of that size (S is above M because small groups waited in review; XL has no merged sample and is 1.5 × L). A group whose fixer is already working gets 70% of its size duration as the remaining estimate. Those are measured lead times, not effort: review rounds and queueing are inside them, so the slot schedule is an upper bound on closure. The batching window is 0 minutes — merge as soon as a batch is ready — because closure is the first objective; the measured trade is in <code>durations.json</code>.</p>
</section>
<section><h2>Dependency depth</h2><p>Derived from the roster's <code>after</code> edges, one level after the deepest open dependency; level 1 is the frontier. Read from plan.json. The hand-cut plan/WAVES.json is retired: it named 39 of 96 groups and left 16 open groups in no wave at all.</p><table><thead><tr><th>level</th><th>open groups</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="mono">1</td><td><span class="tw live" title="in-progress">NIGHT-FOLDS</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress">SAV-REASONS</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress">REPLAY-LANE</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress">FREQ-DEFROST</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress">TRAIN-HOLD</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress">CI-LAYOUT</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">I5-DOCS</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">DEEPLINK-HANDLERS</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">ROSTER-OPS</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">RCA-FRICTION</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">DEPENDABOT-AIOHTTP</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">HANDOFF-ARCHIVE</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">MERGE-PR-MANDATE</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">CI-RATCHET-RED</span><span class="tw live" title="in-progress, queued for a slot">PREPR-CAP</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">BRIEFS-FOLD</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">POLICY-GATE-SCOPING</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">MERGE-SUBJECT-HARDEN</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">POLICY-LINT-FAMILY</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">UPDATE-PR-SIGNALS</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">BUFFER-STORE</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">LEARNER-DEFAULT</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">COP-PARTLOAD</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">MUTANT-SKIP</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">MUTATION-ANCHOR</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">DEMAND-OVERBOOK</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">SAV-COMFORT</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 1">THERMAL-POWER-OPTION</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">2</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">ADVISOR</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">SOLVER</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">RATIO-ANCHOR</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">REPLAY-SCOPED</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">POLICY-FIXER-MD</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">ORCH-MACHINERY</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">RCA-HEADMOVED</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">LOOP-CPU</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">CARD-VOICE</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 2">CEILING-PROBE</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">3</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 3">INPUT-STALENESS</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 3">SCORES</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">4</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 4">CURRENCY</span><span class="tw partial" title="part merged #2379, residual open">SENSOR-PAYLOAD</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 4">LIVESTATE</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">5</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 5">CONFIG-NOTICES</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">6</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 6">PARAMS-OWNER</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">7</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 7">ARCH-SHAPES</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">8</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 8">LEARNER-ETA</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">9</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 9">HEAT-METER</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">10</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 10">COP-GATE</span><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 10">CONFIGFLOW-PAGES</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">11</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 11">UX-HEALTH</span></td></tr><tr><td class="mono">12</td><td><span class="tw ready" title="ready · depth 12">ARCH-DOCS</span></td></tr></tbody></table></section><section><h2>Waves</h2><p>Waves overlap. A wave is the set of groups dispatched at one moment, and the next opens as soon as one of the six pull-request slots frees — the previous wave does not have to drain first. The cap still binds, so overlap cannot put more than six groups in flight; what it costs is a recarry whenever main moves between merges, which the train absorbs anyway. A patch stamp is cut once five production groups have landed and never blocks a dispatch. Every row below is the plan model's output.</p><table><thead><tr><th>wave</th><th>opens (UTC)</th><th>last merge (UTC)</th><th>groups</th><th>stamp it cuts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="mono">1</td><td class="mono">Tue 20 Oct 21:46</td><td class="mono">Wed 21 Oct 18:54</td><td>CI-LAYOUT, FREQ-DEFROST, NIGHT-FOLDS, REPLAY-LANE, SAV-REASONS, TRAIN-HOLD</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr><td class="mono">2</td><td class="mono">Wed 21 Oct 05:45</td><td class="mono">Wed 21 Oct 17:09</td><td>ADVISOR, BRIEFS-FOLD, SOLVER</td><td class="mono">v7.0.3</td></tr><tr><td class="mono">3</td><td class="mono">Wed 21 Oct 06:56</td><td class="mono">Wed 21 Oct 20:02</td><td>RATIO-ANCHOR, REPLAY-SCOPED</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr><td class="mono">4</td><td class="mono">Wed 21 Oct 17:09</td><td class="mono">Thu 22 Oct 13:15</td><td>DEEPLINK-HANDLERS, I5-DOCS, SCORES</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr><td class="mono">5</td><td class="mono">Wed 21 Oct 18:20</td><td class="mono">Thu 22 Oct 07:26</td><td>INPUT-STALENESS</td><td class="mono">—</td></tr><tr><td c